he water is emptied and the unit cleaned between uses."],"answer":["D"]},{"id":12,"category":"נ״ט בר נ״ט","type":"single","prompt":"A can of plain vegetables lists only parve ingredients but has no supervision. Why does the course rule say not to choose it merely because the ingredients are parve?","choices":["Because parve vegetables automatically become dairy equipment.","Because shared or recycled processing water can carry non-kosher taste, and נ״ט בר נ״ט does not help with inherently forbidden taste.","Because canned vegetables are treated as דבר חריף.","Because any sealed food owned by a non-Jew is forbidden."],"answer":["B"]},{"id":13,"category":"Fish & Meat","type":"single","prompt":"Fish and meat were baked at the same time in separate pans in one oven. There was no meaningful steam transfer. What is the course rule?","choices":["It is permitted לכתחילה because the foods never touched.","It is forbidden even בדיעבד because fish and meat can never share an oven.","It should be avoided לכתחילה because of ריחא, but בדיעבד it is generally permitted absent meaningful steam transfer.","It is permitted only if the fish was cooked first."],"answer":["C"]},{"id":14,"category":"Fish & Meat","type":"single","prompt":"After eating fish, what should be done before eating meat according to the course S”A/Rama comparison?","choices":["S”A says only eat and drink; Rama requires washing hands and cleaning the mouth.","S”A says wash hands and clean the mouth; Rama does not require those washings but says it is best to eat and drink between them.","Both require washing hands, cleaning the mouth, eating, and drinking.","Neither requires any separation practice."],"answer":["B"]},{"id":15,"category":"Fish & Meat","type":"truefalse","prompt":"True or False: The course’s majority/practical line says fish and meat may never be on the same table at the same time.","choices":["True","False"],"answer":["B"]},{"id":16,"category":"Fish & Meat","type":"single","prompt":"A piece of fish was cooked in chicken soup. You remove it and rinse it thoroughly. What is the course result for the fish?","choices":["The fish becomes permitted because rinsing removes the meat concern.","The fish is permitted only if it is rinsed three times.","The fish is permitted because fish-and-meat is only a surface-contact concern.","The fish itself is forbidden; rinsing cannot remove the absorbed soup flavor."],"answer":["D"]},{"id":17,"category":"Fish & Meat","type":"single","prompt":"Fish accidentally entered meat food, but there is ששים against the fish. Which statement matches the course positions?","choices":["Maharil permits bitul for סכנה, Issur VeHeiter forbids it, and the course custom is stringent.","Both Maharil and Issur VeHeiter say bitul never applies to סכנה.","Maharil says bitul does not apply to סכנה; Issur VeHeiter permits; the practical custom in the course is lenient.","The course custom is lenient only when there is no ששים."],"answer":["C"]},{"id":18,"category":"Fish & Meat","type":"single","prompt":"In the course discussion of an accidental fish/meat mixture with no ששים, which authority/reasoning pair is correct?","choices":["Magen Avraham questions whether the danger applies today, and Divrei Malkiel can extend that consideration even to an actual mixture.","Maharil permits adding היתר to every accidental rabbinic mixture, and S”A says bitul never applies to סכנה.","Issur VeHeiter says the basic soup is automatically permitted even without ששים.","Pitchei Teshuvah says אין מבטלין איסור לכתחילה unquestionably governs סכנה in every case."],"answer":["A"]},{"id":19,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"Clean ben-yomo meat and dairy vessels are together in hot parve water with no ששים. What is the course S”A/Rama result?","choices":["Both forbid.","Both permit.","S”A forbids; Rama permits.","S”A permits; Rama forbids."],"answer":["D"]},{"id":20,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"In the same clean-vessel hot-water case, one of the two vessels is eino-ben-yomo. What is the course result?","choices":["S”A permits and Rama forbids.","S”A forbids and Rama permits.","Both forbid.","Both permit."],"answer":["D"]},{"id":21,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"A clean ben-yomo meat vessel is placed in hot parve water and removed. Only afterward is a clean ben-yomo dairy vessel placed into that water. What is the course result?","choices":["Both S”A and Rama permit.","S”A permits and Rama forbids.","S”A forbids and Rama permits.","Both forbid unless there is ששים."],"answer":["A"]},{"id":22,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"Parve soup is cooking in a clean ben-yomo dairy pot, and a clean ben-yomo meat ladle is used in the soup. There is no ששים. What is the course S”A/Rama result?","choices":["Both permit.","S”A permits; Rama forbids absent ששים.","S”A forbids; Rama permits.","Both forbid."],"answer":["B"]},{"id":23,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"Dirty meat and dairy dishes are together in a true כלי שני. Which statement matches the course rule?","choices":["The Rama forbids and all later authorities agree.","The Rama permits, although some later authorities are cautious in modern applications.","The Rama permits only if both dishes are clean.","The case is governed only by whether there is ששים."],"answer":["B"]},{"id":24,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"עירוי כלי ראשון is poured onto dirty meat and dairy dishes. Which statement is correct?","choices":["Rama and Shach both permit because עירוי never transfers taste.","Rama permits; Shach forbids because עירוי can cook/transfer כדי קליפה.","Rama forbids; Shach permits because the stream is disconnected.","Both forbid only if the dishes are ben-yomo."],"answer":["B"]},{"id":25,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"A continuous stream of hot parve soup is poured directly from a clean ben-yomo meat pot into a cold dairy bowl. Which answer gives the course status?","choices":["Pot forbidden; soup forbidden; bowl forbidden according to both Rama and Shach.","Pot permitted; soup forbidden; bowl permitted according to both Rama and Shach.","Pot and soup permitted; bowl permitted according to Rama and forbidden according to Shach.","Pot and soup permitted; bowl forbidden according to Rama and permitted according to Shach."],"answer":["D"]},{"id":26,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"A hot solid potato is removed from a clean meat pot and placed on a clean dairy plate. What is the taught rule?","choices":["Forbidden according to the Rama because the potato is still hot.","Permitted only according to S”A.","Forbidden unless the plate is eino-ben-yomo.","Permitted even under the Rama’s taught rule."],"answer":["D"]},{"id":27,"category":"Dishes, Sinks & Dishwashers","type":"single","prompt":"A meat sink clogs and